From 397f3f3e7a806c4e4c2996e5410f99c0a94f7f2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:31:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Show the encryption and disappearing-messages notices of
 a new personal chat

WhatsApp Web draws "Messages and calls are end-to-end encrypted..." and
the disappearing-messages notice itself; neither arrives as text from
WPPConnect (the encryption event is a bodyless e2e_notification, which
WinZapp keeps out of the conversation on purpose). So the sentences are
WinZapp's own, in two places and client-only:

- Chat info of a personal chat: the full encryption sentence.
- An empty or new personal conversation: the existing "no messages"
  row is extended with the short encryption notice and, only when the
  chat has a disappearing-messages timer running, its duration.

The row is the existing empty_placeholder: one row, text only, so no
index shifts and nothing in pagination, the unread separator or the
tail-append logic changes. A leading row in a conversation that has
history was deliberately not added for that reason.

The encryption notice depends only on the JID being a person's (phone or
@lid), never on an event that may or may not have arrived; groups,
broadcast lists and channels get no claim (channels are not E2E).
An off or unknown timer says nothing instead of "off".
